# Keep this module's local tooling/runtime artifacts out of source control.
# These rules do not untrack already committed files or secure them on disk.
# Commit the authored .tf files, settings.example, user-data.sh, and the provider
# lock file; .terraform.lock.hcl is intentionally not ignored.

# Downloaded providers and backend/module metadata generated by terraform init.
# This is a disposable local cache, not authored infrastructure to document/edit.
# Recreate it with init; never commit provider binaries or cached backend settings.
.terraform/
# Local state and state backups can contain identifiers, user data, and sensitive
# values introduced by future resources. Ignore does not encrypt, lock, or back up
# state; shared deployments need an appropriately protected state backend.
*.tfstate*
# Local HCL/JSON input values are account-specific and can contain credentials.
# The documented workflow uses terraform.tfvars; the public .example stays tracked.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
# Saved binary plans and JSON exports can contain sensitive deployment
# configuration. Store/review them privately; never use an old plan blindly.
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.*
# Terraform crash diagnostics may contain environment/configuration details.
crash.log
# Generated outputs consumed by ../taskflow.py publish --settings. Contains
# infrastructure metadata/secret ARNs, not the secret values; regenerate from the
# intended deployment and keep local rather than publishing to the repository.
deployment.json
